HST Office: File-table version floor, so upgrading from beta 1-4 installs every program file again.

beta 1-4 stamped HST's .exe/.dll with the engine version 26.8.1.1; later builds carry the HST version
(1.0.0.500 for beta.5). Windows Installer costs each component against the file already on disk: a
key file with a higher installed version keeps the component from being installed ("Disallowing
installation of component ... since the same component with higher versioned keyfile exists"), whatever
the component GUID (the new GUIDs of hst-msi-component-guids.patch did not change this). RemoveExistingProducts
runs after costing and deletes beta.4's copies: of the 177 executables whose version is lower than in
beta.4 (176 HST-built files plus python.exe), soffice.bin, soffice.com, sc, sw and the rest went missing.

New product variable FILEVERSIONFLOOR: an executable (.bin .com .dll .exe .pyd) whose version is below
the floor is listed in the File table with the floor version. The HSTOffice product sets 26.8.1.2,
just above beta 1-4's highest version, so costing installs them; the files keep their own version
resource (Properties still show 1.0.0.x). Merge-module files (the VC runtime) and fonts are not
affected. A later release with genuinely higher versions is compared as usual. Side effect: an explicit
Repair copies these files again, because the file on disk reports a lower version than the table.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

--- a/instsetoo_native/util/openoffice.lst.in
+++ b/instsetoo_native/util/openoffice.lst.in
@@ -106,12 +106,13 @@
             PATCHCODEFILE ooo_patchcodes.txt
             CODEFILENAME codes_hst.txt
             LEGACYUPGRADECODE {4B17E523-5D91-4E69-BD96-7FD81CFA81BB}
             LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMIN 1.0.0.0
             LEGACYUPGRADEVERSIONMAX 1.0.1.0
             COMPONENTGUIDSEED 1.0-hst2
+            FILEVERSIONFLOOR 26.8.1.2
         }
         active          1
         compression     5
         script          setup_osl
         downloadname    HSTOffice_{productversion}_{os}_install_{languages}
         langpackdownloadname    HSTOffice_{productversion}_languagepack_{os}_install_{languages}
--- a/solenv/bin/modules/installer/windows/file.pm
+++ b/solenv/bin/modules/installer/windows/file.pm
@@ -554,6 +554,20 @@
             my ($header, $subversion, $version, $vervariant, $microversion) = ($1,unpack( "vvvv", $2));
             $fileversion = $version . "." . $subversion . "." . $microversion . "." . $vervariant;
         }
+        # FILEVERSIONFLOOR: the File table lists executables older than the floor with the floor version,
+        # so an upgrade over a release whose same-named files carry a higher version still installs them.
+        # Windows Installer otherwise keeps the "newer" installed file at costing, and RemoveExistingProducts
+        # then deletes it. The file on disk keeps its own version resource.
+        my $floor = $allvariables->{'FILEVERSIONFLOOR'};
+        if (( $floor ) && ( $fileversion ne "" ))
+        {
+            if ( $floor !~ /^\d+\.\d+\.\d+\.\d+$/ ) { installer::exiter::exit_program("ERROR: FILEVERSIONFLOOR must be a.b.c.d: $floor", "get_fileversion"); }
+            my @have = split(/\./, $fileversion);
+            my @min = split(/\./, $floor);
+            my $cmp = 0;
+            for ( my $i = 0; $i < 4 && $cmp == 0; $i++ ) { $cmp = $have[$i] <=> $min[$i]; }
+            if ( $cmp < 0 ) { $fileversion = $floor; }
+        }
     }
     # file version for font files (tdf#76239)
     if ( $onefile->{'Name'} =~ /\.(otf|ttf|ttc)$/i )
